{"timestamp": 1779341674.13699, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 10, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779341697.5978978, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I found Eve's body in Electrical. My path this round was Weapons, then Security, and finally Electrical. Just before I found the body, I was in Security with both Eve and Diana. I saw Diana leave Security and head towards Electrical right before I followed that same path. When I got to Electrical, Diana was gone and Eve was dead on the floor. \n\nDiana, you were heading exactly where the body was found right before me. Did you see what happened, or was there anyone else around? I'd like to hear everyone's paths, but Diana has a lot of explaining to do."}}
{"timestamp": 1779341713.3102305, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Whoa, Charlie, nice try with the self-report. Yes, I was in Security with both of you, but I left *before* you and Eve. I passed through Electrical\u2014which was completely empty\u2014on my way to Medbay to do my submit scan task. The last time I saw Eve, she was alive and well in Security... alone with YOU. \n\nIf she ended up dead in Electrical right after that, it means she followed my path, and you were right behind her. You must have killed her the second she walked into Electrical and immediately reported to frame me because you knew I had just walked that way. I'm voting Charlie, this is a clear setup."}}
{"timestamp": 1779341737.4414785, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I've been completely isolated down in the south side of the ship this whole round. I started in Storage and then headed over to Navigation to do my task. I haven't crossed paths with anyone, so I unfortunately can't directly verify or debunk either of your stories.\n\nThat being said, we clearly have a hard 1v1 situation between Charlie and Diana. One of them is almost certainly the Duck. Diana claims she went from Security through Electrical to Medbay, while Charlie claims he was in Security with both of them before following to Electrical. \n\nAlice and Frank, did either of you happen to see Diana in Medbay, or Charlie in Weapons or Security? If anyone can corroborate even a piece of their paths, it would crack this wide open. Let's hear from the rest of the group before we lock in our votes, but I think our Duck is definitely one of those two."}}
{"timestamp": 1779341761.112219, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I started my route in Electrical, moved through Medbay, and then headed up to Upper Engine where I was doing my task. I honestly haven't seen a single person this entire round. \n\nDiana, I didn't see you in Medbay. Depending on the timing, I might have already left for Upper Engine by the time you got there, so I unfortunately can't verify or debunk your story. \n\nBob is right\u2014this is a hard 1v1 between Charlie and Diana. One of them is definitely our Duck. Alice, you're the last to speak, and we really need to hear if you saw anything on the right side of the ship near Security or Weapons. Because I don't have any concrete evidence of my own and I have to cast my vote right now without hearing Alice's information, I'm going to skip. I'd rather not flip a coin on a 1v1 if Alice happens to have the definitive proof we need.\n\nskip"}}
{"timestamp": 1779341838.6812823, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 10, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I was completely on the top left side of the ship this round. My path was Upper Engine, up to Oxygen, and then over to Cafeteria where I was when the meeting was called. I didn't see a single person the entire time, so I have absolutely no information to help break this tie between Charlie and Diana. \n\nSince Frank already skipped and Bob couldn't verify anything from the south either, this is a pure 50/50 for the rest of us. With 5 of us still alive and only 1 Duck, we aren't at match point yet. If we guess wrong today, we risk voting out a Goose for no reason. I think the safest play is to skip, stick together in groups next round, and let the Duck make a mistake. Charlie and Diana, we'll be watching both of you very closely.\n\nskip"}}
